---
description: Steve's defaults: routing to principles and runbooks, prose, push, agent messages
alwaysApply: true
---


- Lead with the shortest complete answer. One recommendation with a reason. Ask only when the answer changes what you do.
- Before your first task in a session, and again after a compaction, read `~/.steez/repo/principles/README.md` and `~/.steez/repo/runbooks/README.md`, then the repo's own `principles/` and `runbooks/` if it has them. Repo wins on conflict. Apply each principle whose apply-when matches. A runbook whose trigger matches supplies your todolist.
- When Steve corrects how you work, read `~/.steez/repo/principles/encode-lessons-in-structure.md` before replying.
- All prose goes through the unslop skill. Invoke it if it isn't loaded yet.
- Push as you commit. The repo says whether main takes direct commits or a PR. Never force-push, and never discard work you did not create.
- When messaging another agent across sessions, start with `[from: <your name or model> @ <herdr pane id>]`, pane id from `HERDR_PANE_ID` or omitted. A message without that prefix is from Steve.
